        "original_id": "3bce691a-8f21-50b3-b566-5ba900ecf158",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Samuel Rickards\n- Organizations: Church of England, Trinity Episcopal Church (Houghton, Michigan)\n- Movements: Oxford Movement\n- Concepts: Anglo-Catholicism, devotional literature\n\nFacts:\n- Samuel Rickards was born in 1796 and died in 1865.\n- Samuel Rickards was a Church of England clergyman.\n- Samuel Rickards opposed the Oxford Movement.\n- Samuel Rickards was a writer of devotional literature.\n- The Oxford Movement was a movement of High Church members of the Church of England.\n- The Oxford Movement eventually developed into Anglo-Catholicism.\n- Trinity Episcopal Church in Houghton, Michigan, has a philosophy built on the Oxford Movement.",
